comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T00:20:00.805Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status PM search for audited extension settings mutation found related closed workspace-audit and SDK audits but no current owner of this missing host-bound contract. GitHub #1345 cites pm-presets pm-1vx6 in that package's tracker; that is a separate consumer defect."
  "2026-09-29T04:56:31.683Z","harness:codex","Test-audit contract: a copied extension with no locally resolvable pm SDK can atomically mutate governed settings through its injected host SDK while retaining strict workspace history. Existing direct SDK singleton tests do not prove extension portability or failure compensation. Primary proof will use a disposable packed consumer."
  "2026-09-29T06:50:38.926Z","harness:codex","Acceptance evidence: extension command SDK now exposes mutateWorkspaceSettings with a fixed host tracker path, lock-scoped read/validate/write, workspace history, author attribution, dry-run, and replay-safe operation IDs. Copied extension integration runs without a local SDK and passes strict health/history verification. Source-level tests cover preview, replay, no-op, invalid current/result, drift, and history failure compensation. Linked tests passed; full suite 9414 passed; exact V8 coverage 100/100/100/100; pnpm quality:static passed. Public SDK surface snapshot acknowledges the added host capability and optional controls."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T06:50:39.821Z","harness:codex",Copied extensions must receive governed workspace mutations through host-injected SDK services; resolving local SDK packages or writing settings.json directly breaks portability and audit attribution.
